// P3G.3 (derived-and-linking.md DV1.9; external-references.md ER6.7 "Open linked document"):
// opening a linked reference's source at its version, read-only. Document B "Block consumer"
// with two instances of A@V1 in Assembly 1 (`linked-block consumer 2`) and "Drawing 1" (a Front
// view of A@V1); A "Block source" then edited to 40 and versioned V2 (`linked-block edit`), so
// its workspace is not what B references.
// 01 (ER6.7) right-click Part 1 <1> → "Open linked document" hovered.
// 02 (DV1.9) Block source at V1, read-only: its tab "Block" active and Part 1 selected (the Parts
//    list, the part highlighted), 25 high (V1; its workspace is 40); the top bar reads "V1"
//    instead of "Main"; the blue banner "Viewing V1 of Block source (read-only). Edits are
//    turned off." with "Back to Block consumer"; the toolbar greyed.
// 03 an edit refused: Extrude 1 double-clicked → the toast "V1 of Block source is open
//    read-only: it can't be edited. Go back to Block consumer to edit." and no dialog.
// 04 Ctrl+Z and the tab menu's Duplicate refused the same way.
// 05 mass properties at V1 (reading is allowed): 37 500 mm³.
// 06 "Back to Block consumer": Assembly 1 as it was (its two instances, the badges).
// 07 the tab menu of Assembly 1: "Open linked document (Block source (V1))" hovered.
// 08 a linked icon clicked → the Reference manager → Selective update: each row's "Open linked
//    document" button (V1, read-only) hovered.
// 09 opened from the manager: Block source at V1 again; Back.
// 10 Drawing 1, the Sheets pane: right-click the reference → "Open linked document" hovered.
// 11 (ER3, same document) "Exercise: Move to Document" with its six pistons at V1 of the same
//    document (`move-doc setup`, `move-doc version-ref`): right-click Piston Assembly <1> →
//    Open linked document.
// 12 the same document at V1, read-only, on its "Piston Assembly" tab (a subassembly source:
//    nothing to select); "Viewing V1 of Exercise: Move to Document".
// 13 Back: the Hexapod again, at the workspace.
Scenario(
    start: Some("document"),
    steps: [
        WaitFor("document-shell"),
        Wait(20),
        Custom("linked-block"),
        Wait(60),
        Custom("linked-block consumer 2"),
        Wait(60),
        Custom("linked-block drawing"),
        Wait(60),
        Custom("linked-block edit"),
        Wait(40),
